{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/routing/exception-handling","title":"Route exception handling","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"route-exception-handling","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Route exception handling"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"When a guard, a matcher or a resolver raises a declared exception, this page is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"where you say what happens next: redirect, render a dedicated component, stay"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"put, or carry on. One map per route resolves the "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"union"}]},{"t":"text","text":" of every code those"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"three steps can produce — and the compiler checks that the map is exactly"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"complete, no more and no less."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Use it when"}]},{"t":"text","text":" a route's guards, matchers or resolvers can fail in ways the user"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"should see."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Not when"}]},{"t":"text","text":" the failure is local to one primitive — read it off"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"exceptions()"},{"t":"text","text":" instead, see"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/concepts/exceptions","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Exceptions as values"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]},{"t":"callout","tone":"warning","caption":"Breaking change","children":[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Every handler must use "},{"t":"code","text":"craftExceptionHandler(function* (...) {})"},{"t":"text","text":". Internal"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"redirects use "},{"t":"code","text":"yield* redirectTo({ to, params, queryParams, viewTransition })"},{"t":"text","text":";"},{